WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.888
Today is rhymes. Two words rhyme when they sound the same at the end.

2
00:00:04.338 --> 00:00:06.917
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

3
00:00:07.417 --> 00:00:09.496
Say the name of every picture first.

4
00:00:09.946 --> 00:00:11.882
Listen to the end of these two words.

5
00:00:12.332 --> 00:00:12.846
Cat.

6
00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:15.681
Hat.

7
00:00:18.003 --> 00:00:20.876
Cat and hat sound the same at the end. They rhyme.

8
00:00:21.676 --> 00:00:25.272
Cat and leg do not sound the same at the end. They do not rhyme.

9
00:00:26.072 --> 00:00:31.691
With your child, say the two words one after the other. Cat, hat. Let them hear it before you ask.

10
00:00:32.141 --> 00:00:37.904
Your child circles the picture that rhymes with the first one. Do the four boxes of job one together.

11
00:00:38.354 --> 00:00:46.094
In job two, your child draws a line from each picture to the one that rhymes with it. Then checks the answers upside down.

12
00:00:46.544 --> 00:00:56.224
Rhyme comes slowly for some children. If it does not come today, do this day once more tomorrow. Then go on anyway, and read the rhyme story on day nine.
